Package: nvidia-n1x-dkms-@NVIDIA_BRANCH@-open
Version: @DEB_VERSION@
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: Brandon Sneed <brandon@redf.net>
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/bsneed/n1x-kernel-ubuntu
Depends: dkms, nvidia-kernel-common-@NVIDIA_BRANCH@ (>= @NVIDIA_VERSION@), nvidia-kernel-common-@NVIDIA_BRANCH@ (<= @NVIDIA_VERSION@-1)
Provides: nvidia-dkms-kernel, nvidia-dkms-@NVIDIA_BRANCH@-open (= @NVIDIA_VERSION@)
Conflicts: nvidia-dkms-kernel, nvidia-dkms-@NVIDIA_BRANCH@-open
Replaces: nvidia-dkms-kernel, nvidia-dkms-@NVIDIA_BRANCH@-open
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Description: NVIDIA @NVIDIA_VERSION@ open kernel modules with NVIDIA N1x fixes (DKMS)
 NVIDIA's open GPU kernel modules built from the full source tree through DKMS,
 with Omarchy's NVIDIA N1x patches (two displays behind one USB4 dock port,
 DisplayPort link recovery through USB4 tunnels, USB-C outputs reported as
 DisplayPort, eDP 1.5 OLED brightness, a semaphore callback leak) and a fix
 that lets the N1x GPU go through system suspend.
 .
 Replaces Ubuntu's nvidia-dkms-@NVIDIA_BRANCH@-open for Ubuntu's NVIDIA
 @NVIDIA_VERSION@ user space (any Ubuntu revision), which it must match.
